1	option	About Will and Anne...
2	line	Player	About Will and Anne...
2	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Those plundering seadogs! Did you speak to Ribs about them?
2	line	Player	I did. He seems to think they might have unleashed some sort of curse.
2	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Ah, the curse of Barnacle Barnaby! It's one of Ribs' favourite tales. Just a myth of course, but the old dog does love his stories.
2	line	Player	Well, myths aside, Ribs mentioned you'd put a bounty out for Will and Anne. I'd be quite keen to track them down myself.
2	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Yo ho ho! A mighty good decision! It's a generous bounty indeed. You don't go breaking the one rule of the Pandemonium and expect to get away with it!
2	select	Select an option
2	option	What exactly is this one rule you keep mentioning?
3	line	Player	What exactly is this one rule you keep mentioning?
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Avast! The mainland kingdoms have no authority here. Their laws do not apply. Instead, we just have our one rule that keeps the Pandemonium afloat: Never disrespect your fellow patron.
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	We don't care who you are. Indeed, pirates and customs officers can enjoy a drink here, side by side. Savvy?
3	line	Player	So anyone is welcome here as long as they don't commit an offense against any of the other patrons?
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Yarr! You've got it!
3	line	Player	I see. So, back to Will and Anne. Do you have any idea where they might have gone?
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Shiver me timbers! I'm afraid not. Old Grog said he might try and track them down. Perhaps he has an idea of where to find them.
3	action	below
2	option	Do you have any idea where Will and Anne might have gone?
3	line	Player	Do you have any idea where Will and Anne might have gone?
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Shiver me timbers! I'm afraid not. Old Grog said he might try and track them down. Perhaps he has an idea of where to find them.
3	line	Player	And where would I find Old Grog?
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Ah, the old scallywag left not that long ago, but he'll be back here before long. He enjoys a drink far too much! In the meantime, you should hoist the sails and ready your vessel!
3	line	Player	But I don't have a vessel...
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	What? But then how did you get here?
3	line	Player	Will and Anne threw me overboard and I washed up here. I did mention this earlier...
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Blistering barnacles! Well, you won't be getting far without a boat of your own. You should head to the docks and speak with Junior Jim, our local shipwright. He'll get you sorted out.
3	line	Player	Alright, I'll go and see him.
3	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Jolly Roger!
3	action	end
