0	section	Talking to Junior Jim
1	line	Junior Jim	Can I help you, mate?
1	line	Player	Are you Junior Jim?
1	line	Junior Jim	That's me. What do you need then?
1	line	Player	Steve said you might be able to sort me out with a boat.
1	line	Junior Jim	You don't have a boat?
1	line	Player	No.
1	line	Junior Jim	Ha! We've got ourselves a Billy-no-boats! Classic! Yeah, I can sort you out with a boat, but it's gonna cost you.
1	line	Player	How much?
1	line	Junior Jim	Well, what do you have?
1	line	Player	Er... I do have this cup I found. Perhaps I could trade it for a boat.
1	line	Junior Jim	Alright, let's have a gander at it.
1	cond	If the player lost the old cup:
2	line	Player	I seem to have lost it.
2	line	Junior Jim	You've got no boat. You've got no cup. You're fresh out of luck it would seem, mate. You'd best hope you lost it here on the Pandemonium. If so, someone might have handed it in to Steve.
2	line	Player	Then I guess I'd better go see if Steve has it.
2	action	end
1	box	You show the cup to Junior Jim.
1	line	Junior Jim	Hmm... Yeah, yeah, I can work with this. This old rusty cup will get you the finest raft I have!
1	line	Player	Sorry, I think I must have misheard you. Did you say raft?
1	line	Junior Jim	That's right! The best one I have!
1	line	Player	I was kind of hoping for a bit more than a raft. It's not just the cup I have. I'm sure I can make up the funds to buy something bigger.
1	line	Junior Jim	Sorry, mate, but even if you could, the raft is all I've got to hand right now. Besides, you're gonna want to build up some experience before you captain anything too big. A raft will be perfect for you.
1	line	Player	Okay...
1	line	Junior Jim	Lighten up, mate. I'll have plenty more vessels in stock soon. Come back once you've got a bit more know-how and I'll be able to sort you right out.
1	line	Junior Jim	Now, about your raft... With that cup I'll be able to sort you out with the finest helm, but it won't be enough to cover the sails.
1	line	Player	But I won't get anywhere without sails!
1	line	Junior Jim	Don't panic, you silly plonker. I ain't about to send you off on a raft with no sails. I'll sort them out for you, but I'll just need a little favour in return.
1	line	Player	What favour?
1	line	Junior Jim	I've got some cargo I need picking up from Port Sarim and bringing back here. In return for sorting you out with some sails, I'll need you to go and collect it for me.
1	line	Junior Jim	Oh, and I tell you what, I'll even set you up with the materials to whack together a cargo hold. You won't be shifting that cargo far without one.
1	line	Player	Thanks!
1	line	Junior Jim	Now, hand over that cup and we can get cracking.
1	box	You give the cup to Junior Jim.
1	line	Junior Jim	Right, time to sort you out with a cargo hold. Let's head on over to the shipyard...
1	line	Junior Jim	You'll want to grab yourself some tools from the crates over there, mate. After that, just use the gangplank to hop onto your raft. Once you're on board, you can get to work.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Junior Jim again before showing him the cup or using the cup on him
1	line	Junior Jim	You're back! Do you have that cup? If so, let's have a gander at it.
1	cond	If the player lost the cup:
2	line	Player	I seem to have lost it.
2	line	Junior Jim	You've got no boat. You've got no cup. You're fresh out of luck it would seem, mate. You'd best hope you lost it here on the Pandemonium. If so, someone might have handed it in to Steve.
2	line	Player	Then I guess I'd better go see if Steve has it.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player has the cup:
2	line	Junior Jim	Hmm... Yeah, yeah, I can work with this. This old rusty cup will get you the finest raft I have!
2	action	above
