0	section	Modify Boat Schematics before building the cargo hold
1	box	This is the schematics board. It's used to upgrade core parts of your boat, such as the hull. However, you have no reason to use it right now. You should focus on building your cargo hold instead.
1	action	end
0	section	Building the Cargo hold
1	box	Junior Jim helpfully provides the materials required to build the cargo hold.
1	line	Junior Jim	Very nice! Now, use the gangplank to hop back up here and we can get going.
1	action	end
0	section	Attempting to modify the cargo hold
1	box	It doesn't seem like a good idea to modify anything right now.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Junior Jim again
1	line	Junior Jim	Smashing job on that cargo hold, mate. Let's get back to the Pandemonium, shall we?
1	line	Junior Jim	Okay, looks like that's you all sorted, mate. I'd say you're now ready to set sail!
1	line	Player	How exciting!
1	line	Junior Jim	Why don't you take your new raft out for a spin? You can head over to Port Sarim and collect that cargo for me. Oh, which reminds me, now that you're officially a captain, you'll need one of these.
1	cond	If the player has no inventory space:
2	box	Junior Jim tries to give you a log book, but you don't have enough room to take it.
2	line	Junior Jim	Ah, seems you don't have room for it, mate. Why don't you come back later?
2	action	end
1	box	Junior Jim gives you a log book.
1	line	Junior Jim	Your very own captain's log! You can use that to keep track of your adventures out at sea, including any work you might end up taking on.
1	line	Player	Like collecting your cargo?
1	line	Junior Jim	Right on, mate! In fact, I'll make a note of that in your log now.
1	box	Junior Jim updates your log with details on his request. You can consult the log at any point for a reminder on what he needs you to do.
1	line	Junior Jim	And that's you all ready to go, mate! Just hop on your new raft when ready. If you need help finding my cargo, just check in with the port master when you get to Port Sarim.
1	line	Junior Jim	Now, unless you fancy a cheeky dip, the gangplank down the docks will be your best bet for getting on board.
1	box	You can embark or disembark from your boat via docking points found around the world. To find a docking point, just look for the relevant icon on your map.
1	action	end
