0	section	Talking to Junior Jim after depositing the cargo
1	line	Junior Jim	Alright, mate.
1	line	Player	I collected your cargo and left it with the port master.
1	line	Junior Jim	Very nice! That's us all squared up then. You ought to pop back once you've got a bit more experience with that raft. By then I should have some new vessels for sale.
1	box	Shipwrights like Junior Jim can sell you new boats or help you upgrade your existing ones. To find a shipwright, just look for the relevant icon on your map.
1	line	Player	I might just do that. Any tips on the best ways to get that experience?
1	line	Junior Jim	To be honest, mate, I'd say one of the best things would be to take on more work like what you just did for me. A lot of ports will have a notice board where folks advertise jobs they want sorting.
1	box	Port tasks can be accepted from notice boards found in various ports around the world. To find a notice board, just look for the relevant icon on your map.
1	line	Player	Sounds good. Anything else?
1	line	Junior Jim	Well, now that you're officially a big cheese captain, you might want to start charting the sea for your own records. That log book I gave you has all sorts of cracking tips on how to do so.
1	line	Junior Jim	Oh, and while we're on about charting, I've also chucked some useful bits and bobs in your cargo hold.
1	line	Junior Jim	First up, I've left you a couple of repair kits in there. Perfect for if you go being a numpty and end up sailing straight into a proper big storm or a big group of sharks.
1	line	Junior Jim	The other thing in there is a spyglass. It's a proper handy charting tool that's great for getting a good look at things while out at sea.
1	line	Junior Jim	There's a chap called Charles who used to be pretty good at the whole charting thing who might be able to help you more. You can find him down in the cave on the island.
1	box	Your captain's log contains details on how to chart the sea. You can consult the log at any time for hints on what to chart. Charles in the cave on the Pandemonium can also help you out with sea charting.
1	line	Player	Great! Thanks, Jim. I'd better go check in with Steve now and see if Old Grog is back.
1	line	Junior Jim	Don't mention it, mate.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Steve
1	line	Old Grog	Is this the one?
1	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Aye! This Jolly Roger here is pretty keen to see some justice dealt! Old Grog, meet... er...
1	line	Player	{player}.
1	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	{player}! And {player}, meet Old Grog.
1	line	Player	Pleased to meet you.
1	line	Old Grog	Steve tells me you're keen to see Will and Anne dealt with. I'm open to sharing the bounty, but only if you have what it takes. I have no time for layabouts.
1	line	Player	I won't let you down!
1	line	Old Grog	We'll see. I saw that raft you rocked up in. If that's all you bring to the table, then you have some work to do.
1	line	Old Grog	It will take me some time to track Will and Anne down, but make no mistake, I will find them. I expect you to be ready by the time that happens. Don't be a disappointment.
1	line	Player	You have my word.
1	line	Old Grog	Good. Now, that's me done drinking. Time to get to work. I'll keep Steve updated on my progress, so make sure you're checking in with him. He'll let you know once I have something.
1	box	Old Grog departs.
1	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Yo ho ho, {player}! Best you not waste time! Belay your helm and abaft your rigging! Get out there and make sure you're ready for Old Grog!
1	line	Player	Will do!
1	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	To help you on your way, I've got some pirate looty here for you! Sawmill coupons! Useful if you want a top vessel like mine.
1	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Oh, and don't forget to pop back for a drink from time to time. My rum is to die for! Now, avast!
0	section	Talking to Steve again after Old Grog departs
1	line	'Squawking' Steve Beanie	Yo ho ho, {player}! Best you not waste time! Belay your helm and abaft your rigging! Get out there and make sure you're ready for Old Grog!
1	action	above
